WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.059
You've probably heard, don't put all your eggs in one basket.

2
00:00:05.059 --> 00:00:07.915
Here's what that means for investing.

3
00:00:08.814 --> 00:00:11.121
Here are twenty companies.

4
00:00:11.121 --> 00:00:15.291
Nobody knows which ones will do well this year.

5
00:00:15.291 --> 00:00:17.154
Not even the experts.

6
00:00:18.054 --> 00:00:22.119
A year later, results are all over the place.

7
00:00:22.119 --> 00:00:25.010
One went up thirty-five percent.

8
00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:27.449
Another fell forty percent.

9
00:00:28.349 --> 00:00:34.215
If you put all one thousand dollars into one company, your result is pure luck.

10
00:00:34.215 --> 00:00:39.488
You could end with thirteen hundred fifty dollars, or just six hundred.

11
00:00:40.388 --> 00:00:42.024
Now spread it out.

12
00:00:42.024 --> 00:00:45.477
Fifty dollars into each of the twenty.

13
00:00:46.377 --> 00:00:50.550
The big wins and the big losses mostly cancel out.

14
00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:53.972
You get the average, about eight percent.

15
00:00:53.972 --> 00:00:56.642
One thousand and eighty dollars.

16
00:00:57.542 --> 00:01:02.295
Diversifying doesn't stop the whole market from falling sometimes.

17
00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:06.617
But it protects you from one bad company sinking everything.

18
00:01:07.516 --> 00:01:10.925
Less risk, similar average reward.

19
00:01:10.925 --> 00:01:13.230
That's diversification.

20
00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:17.541
This is for learning, not financial advice.

